@apainintheneck It seems like with these changes, it may happen that for some cases there is now a `service` value of `{}`, which was previously `null`, which the homebrew client can't parse as a service definition.

Given that it happens for the `podman` formula (reported at https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-core/issues/131284), it may only occur if there is no applicable service in the general case, but one of the variations (e.g. linux) provides one: 
https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-core/blob/21a3b1e961b3d78542a683504fd5931720b486e5/Formula/podman.rb#L163C1-L167
